# AI Server Python API docs curation

Full reference: `opentrons-ai-server/docs/API_DOCS_CURATION.md`

## Do not edit generated files

- **Edit:** `api/storage/api_docs/api_docs_struct_about.md` (committed source of truth)
- **Do not edit:** `api_docs_struct.md` (regenerated by `make sync-api-docs`)
- **Do not edit:** `api/storage/api_docs/docs/v2/` (gitignored; synced from pinned `DOCS_TAG`)

## Curated about file format

Each synced markdown path gets one entry:

```markdown
### modules/index.md

<about>
Description for the doc-routing helper model.
</about>
```

## Regenerate after curation changes

```bash
cd opentrons-ai-server
make sync-api-docs              # rebuild api_docs_struct.md
make check-api-docs-curation    # fail if curated entries and synced docs diverge
```

Commit `api_docs_struct_about.md` when `<about>` text changes.

## Adding curation for new mkdocs pages

Add a new entry to `api_docs_struct_about.md` for each synced markdown path, then run sync and the coverage check.

`<about>` text must help `get_relevant_api_docs` route queries: concepts covered, robot types, doc vs protocol file.

## Required curation

Every synced markdown file must have a curated entry. Sync fails if any are missing. `make check-api-docs-curation` and CI also fail on gaps.

## Alerting

- **Sync failure:** missing curated entries block `make sync-api-docs`
- **CI + prep:** `make check-api-docs-curation` (fails on gaps)
- **Common trigger:** bumping `DOCS_TAG` when mkdocs adds/renames pages

See `docs/API_DOCS_CURATION.md` section "How you get alerted".
